  16:     - The bar starts at the left edge; its length is the control value n.
  17: 
  18:     Rule:
  19:     - Build a one-dimensional sequence of foreground runs with lengths
  20:       1, 2, ..., n, n-1, ..., 2, 1.
  21:     - Separate adjacent runs by one background pixel.
  22:     - Wrap the sequence row-major across the input width and pad the final row
  23:       with background pixels.
  24: 
  25:     Key insight:
  26:     The output preserves the input width; the bar length controls the run-length
  27:     diamond, and the apparent 2D pattern is just that 1D sequence wrapped into rows.
  28:     """
  29:     g = np.asarray(grid, dtype=int)
  30:     bg = get_bg(g)
  31:     fg_colors = colors_present(g, exclude={bg})
  32:     assert len(fg_colors) == 1, "expected exactly one foreground color"
  33:     color = int(fg_colors[0])
